# tools/ales_stereo_expand_env_witness.rish — stereo_expand_env: the attack/release downward expander carried into stereo, the linked envelope driving one linked widening over time — the stereo time-varying dynamics quartet made whole (ALES164).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES164.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-070944_fill-ales164-lotus-stereo-expand-env.md
# Stands on: lotus/stereo_envelope.rye (ALES160 — the linked envelope, its stereo_env_step reused whole), lotus/stereo_expand.rye (ALES159 — the linked widening this drives over time, its memoryless form the unit-coefficient
# limit), lotus/expand_env.rye (ALES61 — the mono attack/release expander, its ExpandEnvError reused whole and its output the left-always-peak comparison), lotus/expand.rye (ALES60 — the deepened floor),
# lotus/pan.rye (ALES10 — the StereoClip), lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, sample_max).
#
# lotus/stereo_expand_env.rye expands a span of sample-PAIRS in a master below a magnitude threshold by a ratio, the one downward widening following the shared LINKED envelope over time. Each pair advances one shared
# envelope toward the linked peak max(|left|, |right|) by ALES160's step (attack while rising, release while falling): at or above the threshold both pass byte for byte (continuous at the threshold), below it the deepened
# floor exp = max(0, threshold − deficit·num/den) (ALES60's floor on the linked envelope) yields one gain exp/e applied to both raw samples — one detector, one gain, the image held. A shared envelope of exactly zero arises
# only when both channels are silent, so no divide by zero. ExpandEnvError (BadThreshold, BadRatio, BadCoeff, BadRange) reused whole; the fusion adds no fault. Values only, never a length. The crux is the instantaneous law
# (unit attack and release reducing it to ALES159's memoryless stereo_expand byte for byte on both — the time-varying rung's zero-smoothing limit is exactly the memoryless one already proven), the linked-gain-over-time law
# (a left-always-peak master with left' equal to ALES61's mono expand_env(left), the right scaled by the same fraction, the independent per-channel expand_env differing), the image law (the shared gain preserving the L:R
# ratio, an out-of-phase pair returning still out of phase), the knob laws (unit ratio the identity, a slower release easing the widening longer), the carry law (a span in two pieces equal to the whole once on both), and the
# at-threshold/silence/balance/atomicity/degenerate law.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_stereo_expand_env_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-expand-env: Language EN — stereo_expand_env expands a span of sample-pairs in a stereo master below a magnitude threshold by a ratio, the one downward widening following the shared linked envelope over time. Each pair advances one shared envelope toward the linked peak (the max of the two channels' magnitudes, clamped to the rail), the attack fraction while it rises and the release while it falls; where the smoothed envelope sits at or above the threshold the expander is idle and both channels pass byte for byte, and where it falls below, the envelope's deficit is widened by the ratio and the single gain (the deepened floor over the envelope) is applied to both raw samples. It validates the threshold, ratio, attack, release, and span once against the shared length before any write, so a refusal never expands one channel and leaves the other torn. It writes values only, never a length, so the two channels leave balanced; the caller owns the envelope across calls, so a span expanded in two pieces equals the whole once and the release eases across the boundary."
say "ales-stereo-expand-env: Style Radiant — ALES159's stereo_expand leans on a pair the instant it sees it: a pair below the threshold has its deficit widened the moment it arrives, and the widening vanishes the moment the pair rises. A real expander breathes — it hears a sound end and holds through the release before it deepens, so the tail of a note falls smoothly rather than being wrenched down, and the expander does not pump on every dip. ALES160 built exactly that breath for stereo, one shared envelope tracking the linked peak, and proved it once. This rung spends both proofs: it drives the downward widening from the smoothed linked envelope rather than the bare pair, and applies the one resulting gain to both channels — the quiet pushed down together, the image held to the sample the whole time, and with it the stereo time-varying dynamics quartet (compress, gate, limit, expand, each over one linked envelope) is whole. Two proofs fused: the detector is linked and time-smoothed (the louder channel deciding the shared loudness over time), and the gain is linked (one widened gain from the linked envelope applied to both, since expanding each channel by its own envelope would deepen on different samples and tear the image). The crux is six laws: the instantaneous law (unit attack and release making the linked envelope the instantaneous linked peak, so this equals ALES159's memoryless stereo_expand byte for byte on both — the time-varying rung's zero-smoothing limit exactly the memoryless one already proven); the linked-gain-over-time law (a left-always-peak master with the left equal to ALES61's mono expand_env of it byte for byte, the right scaled by the same fraction, the independent per-channel expand_env genuinely differing); the image law (the shared gain preserving the left-to-right ratio, an out-of-phase pair returning still out of phase, no magnitude expanding and no sign flipping); the knob laws (unit ratio the identity everywhere, a slower release easing the widening longer, monotone); the carry law (a span expanded in two pieces equal to expanding the whole once, byte for byte on both); and the at-threshold, silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate law (a master whose linked envelope never falls below the threshold passing byte for byte, silence staying silence, the lengths held, each of the four refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, count zero the identity on both)."
say "ales-stereo-expand-env: Lens TAME — two bounded in-process i16 Clips (left, right) carrying one shared i64 envelope, one linked-peak comparison and at most one widen and one multiply-then-divide for the gain per channel, all in i64 (the product of a magnitude and the deepened floor at most 32768 times 32767 never overflowing), the gain exp over e in the half-open interval zero to one so every scaled magnitude is at most its input's and fits i16; the two channels enter balanced (the StereoClip invariant asserted on entry) and leave balanced (an expander writes values only, each length asserted equal and within bound on exit, each written sign asserted held); the threshold, ratio, both coefficients, and the span are validated once before either channel is mutated, so a refusal never expands one channel and leaves the other torn; the linked envelope is asserted a legal magnitude in zero to sample_max each sample and the deepened floor within zero to envelope, so the single gain is a genuine reduction; a shared envelope of exactly zero arises only when both channels are silent (asserted), so no divide by zero and nothing to expand; StereoExpandEnvError is ALES61's ExpandEnvError (BadThreshold, BadRatio, BadCoeff, BadRange) reused whole, the fusion adding no fault. The instantaneous law is proven by running both stereo_expand_env under unit attack and release and ALES159's memoryless stereo_expand on the same master and demanding byte-for-byte equality on both channels; the linked-gain-over-time law against a master where the left always holds the peak — the left equal to ALES61's mono expand_env of it byte for byte while the right is scaled by the same fraction, the independent mono expand_env of the right alone shown to genuinely differ; the image law proves no magnitude expands and no sign flips over a mixed master and that an out-of-phase pair returns still exactly out of phase; the knob laws prove unit ratio the identity everywhere and a slower release easing a quiet tail where an instant release deepens it; the carry law proves a span expanded in two pieces equal to the whole once on both channels; and the at-threshold, silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate cases prove an always-loud master passing byte for byte, an all-silent master staying zero, the length held, each of the five refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, and an empty span the identity on both; siloed to lotus/, the threshold a magnitude in sample units, the ratio a plain fraction, the attack and release fractions per sample index, no real sample rate, no anti-aliasing, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_expand_env"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_expand_env.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-expand-env: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_expand_env.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-expand-env: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-expand-env: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-expand-env' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-expand-env: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-expand-env line"
